    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Proof. The assumptions imply that µ+ is continuous and strictly increasing and hence is the cumulative mass function of a continuous measure on [0,∞). Moreover, µ+ is a bijection of [0,∞), and its generalized inverse µ−+1 is simply the inverse function. Let ψ0 = ψ, and for n ∈ N, deﬁne ψn recursively by"
